      <div type="clause" n="80.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 80.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 80.2" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="596" ed="#liebermann"/>Si in uia regia fiat assultus super aliquem, forestal<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#Hn_80-2.lnote.oe.b"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Hn_80-2.lnote.oe.9"/> est et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Hn_80-2.lnote.oe.10"/> C sol.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#Hn_80-2.lnote.oe.c"/> emendetur regi, (maxime<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Hn_80-2.lnote.oe.11"/>) si ibi calumpniam habeat, ut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Hn_80-2.lnote.oe.12"/> diuadietur uel retineatur ibi malefactor, uel si est in socna regis.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 596 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_80-2.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">596</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> IV Atr. 4; II Cn. 12; E Cf. 12; Leis Wl 26. <hi rend="italic">Strenger</hi> Très anc. cout. Norm. I 15, 2: Si quis aliquem in quimino assultauerit cum sanguinis effusione, captus membris punietur; et si occiderit, morte moriatur</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. IV Atr. 4; II Cn. 12; E Cf. 12; Leis Wl 26. More severe: Très anc. cout. Norm. I 15, 2: Si quis aliquem in quimino assultauerit cum sanguinis effusione, captus membris punietur; et si occiderit, morte moriatur</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_80-2.lnote.oe.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">596</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 10, 1. 12, 2. 35, 2. 80, 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. 10, 1. 12, 2. 35, 2. 80, 4</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_80-2.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">596</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-tel <hi rend="italic">Sc Hg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-tel Sc Hg</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_80-2.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">596</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in K Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_80-2.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">596</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nicht in Sc Hg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not in Sc Hg</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_80-2.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">596</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">aut <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi> [<hi rend="italic">laut</hi> 80, 6 ut: <hi rend="italic">wenn nämlich</hi>]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">aut Lond [according to 80, 6 ut: namely, if]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_80-2.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Strasse 13. a (anderswo setzt sie Vf. unbedingt unter königliche Gerichtsbarkeit, hier nur unter der Voraussetzung, dass sie entweder Territorium ohne private Gerichtsbarkeit durchziehe, oder die Tat handhaft [<hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> 1; Pfändung 7] sei); Rechtssperrung 4 ff.; Angriff 3—<hi rend="italic">forestel</hi>{9} <hi rend="italic">est C</hi> ohne <hi rend="italic">et</hi>—<hi rend="italic">maxime</hi>{11} <hi rend="italic">aut</hi>{12}—<hi rend="italic">sonna r</hi>. Rs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Strasse 13. a (elsewhere the author places it unconditionally under royal jurisdiction, here only on the condition that it either runs through territory without private jurisdiction, or that the deed is flagrant [<hi rend="italic">see Gl</hi> 1; Pfändung 7]); Rechtssperrung 4 ff.; Angriff 3—<hi rend="italic">forestel</hi>{9} <hi rend="italic">est C</hi> without <hi rend="italic">et</hi>—<hi rend="italic">maxime</hi>{11} <hi rend="italic">aut</hi>{12}—<hi rend="italic">sonna r</hi>. Rs</seg></note>
      </div>
